<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Emirate of Nejd and Hasa</h1><p class="st-meta">1902 CE – 1921 CE · capital Riyadh</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The third Saudi state in its first phase, begun when Ibn Saud recaptured Riyadh in 1902, which defeated the Rashidis and took al-Hasa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In January 1902 the young <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</a>, living in exile in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sheikhdom-of-kuwait">Sheikhdom of Kuwait</a>, captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masmak-fort">Masmak fort</a> from the Rashidi governor with a small band of followers. He gradually reclaimed southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Najd</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-jabal-shammar">Emirate of Jabal Shammar</a>, defeating its emir at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rawdat-muhanna">Rawdat Muhanna</a> in 1906.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> combined tribal diplomacy, marriage alliances and the Wahhabi religious establishment. From about 1912 he settled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> in agricultural communities called hijras, creating the Ikhwan, a militant religious force. In 1913 he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ahsa-oasis">al-Hasa</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, gaining the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Gulf</a> coast. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-darin">Treaty of Darin</a> in 1915 made him a British protégé with a subsidy.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1921 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> conquered Ha'il, ending the Rashidi state, and took the title <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> and its Dependencies, beginning the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sultanate-of-nejd">Sultanate of Nejd</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa.jpg" alt="Emirate of Nejd and Hasa" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: The Shura Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saudi_Arabia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1902 CE – 1921 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Riyadh</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Wahhabi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Emirate of Riyadh, Third Saudi State, Emirate of Nejd (1902-1921)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1912&amp;focus=emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa" aria-label="Emirate of Nejd and Hasa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5921 1271 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Emirate of Nejd and Hasa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6241 1527L6241 1527M6241 1527L5709 970M6241 1527L4997 651M6241 1527L6241 1527"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6241 1527h0M5709 970h0M4997 651h0M6241 1527h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6241 1527h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6241 1527h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Riyadh. <a href="/atlas?year=1912&amp;focus=emirate-of-nejd-and-hasa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
